From e072c497df9c4acf1ae2f0202af9cf100ed3088f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andy1210 <andy1210@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 18:02:51 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 020/149] PCI: qcom: Do not advertise native hot-plug on the
 Root Ports

The Root Ports keep the hardware's Hot-Plug Capable and Hot-Plug Surprise
bits in their Slot Capabilities, although no hot-plug interrupt is wired
up and the endpoints are soldered down (or powered through pwrctrl).

With Hot-Plug Capable set, the port is a hot-plug bridge, and without a
native pciehp the PCI core never moves it to D3hot. During system suspend
the D3cold check then fails at the Root Port, the link stays up and the
controller keeps its clocks, interconnect votes and GDSC on, which keeps
the SoC out of its deep sleep states (e.g. on the Surface Duo 2 with a
WCN6855: "pcie_0_gdsc status stuck at 'on'" on every suspend).

Clear both bits, as is already done for the Attention Button.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c
index 89a476c37098..d4aea99f4b35 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c
@@ -396,6 +396,15 @@ static void qcom_pcie_set_slot_cap(struct dw_pcie *pci)
 	 * Attention Button Present in Slot Capabilities.
 	 */
 	val &= ~PCI_EXP_SLTCAP_ABP;
+
+	/*
+	 * Nor native hot-plug: there is no hot-plug interrupt, and the
+	 * endpoints are soldered down or powered by pwrctrl. Left set, Hot-Plug
+	 * Capable marks the port a hot-plug bridge, which the PCI core never
+	 * puts into D3hot without pciehp, so the link can never reach D3cold
+	 * and the controller stays powered through system suspend.
+	 */
+	val &= ~(PCI_EXP_SLTCAP_HPC | PCI_EXP_SLTCAP_HPS);
 	writel(val, pci->dbi_base + offset + PCI_EXP_SLTCAP);
 
 	dw_pcie_dbi_ro_wr_dis(pci);
